# Project Context
You are an expert Full-Stack Developer utilizing "Vibe Coding" methodology. You are building a "Site Settlement Automation Platform" (Build-Easy) for small construction and interior firms in Korea.

# Core Value Proposition
- Target Users: Site managers who wear gloves and work in dusty environments
- Key UX Goal: "Extreme Simplicity" - Buttons must be large (h-14+), Inputs minimal, Mobile-first design absolute priority
- Core Features: OCR Receipt Scanning, Daily Labor Logs, Site P&L Dashboard
- Language: Korean (ko-KR)

# Tech Stack Rules
- Framework: Next.js 15+ (App Router). Use Server Components by default
- Database: Supabase. Use @supabase/ssr. STRICTLY enforce Row Level Security (RLS)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4. Use shadcn/ui
- Form: react-hook-form + zod
- OCR: Use Vercel AI SDK with GPT-4o for extracting data from receipt images
- Deployment: Vercel

# Coding Style
- Directory: feature-based (e.g., app/(dashboard)/project/[id]/expenses/page.tsx)
- Error Handling: Return structured error objects { success: false, error: string } in Server Actions
- Naming: Kebab-case for files, PascalCase for components
- Immutability: ALWAYS create new objects, NEVER mutate
- File Organization: MANY SMALL FILES > FEW LARGE FILES (200-400 lines typical)

# Database Schema
- projects: id, user_id(owner), name, start_date, budget
- expenses: id, project_id, image_url(receipt), category(material/food/fuel/other), amount, vendor_name, date
- workers: id, user_id(owner), name, daily_wage, phone
- labor_logs: id, project_id, worker_id, work_date, status(full/half)

# "Gloves-on Mode" UI Rules
- Main interaction buttons (Save, Photo, Add): h-14+ (56px+ tall)
- Touch targets: Minimum 44px x 44px
- No complex ERP: Keep it to "Cash In / Cash Out"
- Color coding:
  - Material (자재비): 🟦 Blue (blue-600)
  - Labor (노무비): 🟧 Orange (orange-600)
  - Save/Confirm: 🟩 Dark Green (green-700)
- Inputs: Minimize keyboard usage, use date pickers, OCR auto-fill

# Mobile First Priority
- Use <input type="file" capture="environment"> for camera
- Large fonts: text-xl for numbers, text-lg for labels
- Generous padding: p-4 minimum
- Bottom navigation or fixed action buttons

# Phase Implementation Order
1. Foundation: Next.js 15 + Supabase + Tailwind + Shadcn/UI
2. Auth: Simple email/password login (Kakao in-app browser compatible)
3. Database: Schema with RLS policies
4. OCR Feature: Receipt scanning with AI auto-fill
5. Labor Logs: Calendar UI with worker check-in
6. Dashboard: Project cards with budget vs expense progress bars
